{
  "formatVersion": 2,
  "title": "Heating and cooling",
  "description": "Three rooms in summer, 27 °C inside and 30 °C outside. The office thermostat changes over automatically: above its cooling setpoint (24 °C) it cools, below its heating setpoint (21 °C) it heats. Its two control values reach one change-over valve, which feeds a 2-pipe fan coil with cold or hot water. The meeting-room thermostat starts in heating mode and does nothing: press its Season key, which writes the heating/cooling object (DPT 1.100) as a central summer/winter switch would, and its cooling value opens the valve of the cooling coil. The same key also changes over the classroom, a 2-pipe system with a single control value: its thermostat sends one value for heating or cooling, and the actuator takes hot or cold water from the season object. Lower the outside temperature in the Rooms panel to see the office change over to heating.",
